          "code": "M1",
          "desc": "Evaluate $f(0) = 2.5 - a^0$"
        },
        {
          "code": "A1",
          "desc": "State the coordinates of $P$"
        }
      ],
      "solution": "$f(0) = 2.5 - a^0 = 2.5 - 1 = 1.5 \\quad \\{a > 0\\}$. Therefore, $P$ has coordinates $(0, 1.5)$.",
      "ai_explanation": {
        "concept_rule": "Point $P$ is the $y$-intercept where $x = 0$.",
        "step_by_step": [
          "Substitute $x = 0$ into $f(x) = 2.5 - a^x$.",
          "Use $a^0 = 1$ to get $f(0) = 2.5 - 1 = 1.5$.",
          "State coordinates as $(0, 1.5)$."
        ],
        "common_pitfalls": "Forgetting that $a^0 = 1$ for any $a > 0$."
      }
    },
    {
      "subpart": "b",
      "stem": "Find the value of $a$.",
      "final_answer": "$a = 2$",
      "mark_breakdown": [
